149\t## Dependency Review Expectations\n   150\t\n   151\tYalla pulls only what 
it needs. When you add or update a third-party\n   152\tGo module, follow the ch
ecklist in\n   153\t[`CONTRIBUTING.md`](./CONTRIBUTING.md#dependency-review-chec
klist) and\n   154\texpect the dependency-review CI job to gate the PR. New modu
les with\n   155\tunknown licenses or known high-severity advisories will be rej
ected\n   156\tautomatically.\n   157\t\n   158\t## Container Image Hardening\n 
 159\t\n   160\tThe production `Dockerfile` ships the `yalla-api` binary and\n  
161\t`Dockerfile.worker` ships the `yalla-worker` binary inside a\n   162\t`gcr.
io/distroless/static-debian12:nonroot` runtime so a leaked or\n   163\tcompromis
ed image carries no shell, no package manager, no busybox,\n   164\tand no setui
d binaries — only the service binary and the system CA\n   165\tbundle. The hard
ening posture is part of the public contract and is\n   166\tpinned by `internal
/release/container_hardening_static_test.go`; a\n   167\tregression in any one o
f the following is caught at build time:\n   168\t\n   169\t- **Multi-stage buil
d.** The Go toolchain, module cache, and source\n   170\t  tree never reach the 
runtime layer. A single-stage Dockerfile is\n   171\t  rejected.\n   172\t- **Di
stroless `nonroot` runtime.** The runtime stage\'s base image\n   173\t  is pinn
ed to `gcr.io/distroless/static-debian12:nonroot` (UID/GID\n   174\t  65532). De
bian/Ubuntu/Alpine slim runtimes are rejected because\n   175\t  they reintroduc
e a shell and a package manager.\n   176\t- **`USER nonroot:nonroot`.** The runt
ime stage MUST run as the\n   177\t  non-root user. A missing or partial (`USER 
nonroot`) directive is\n   178\t  rejected.\n   179\t- **Hardened build flags.**
The builder stage MUST invoke\n   180\t  `go build` with `CGO_ENABLED=0` (static
binary compatible with\n   181\t  the distroless static image), `-trimpath` (str
ip local filesystem\n   182\t  paths from the binary), and `-ldflags="-s -w"` (d
rop the symbol\n   183\t  and DWARF tables). Each missing flag is a separate reg
ression.\n   184\t- **No `ADD <url>`.** Fetching arbitrary content at build time
\n   185\t  without checksum verification is forbidden. Use `COPY` or a\n   186\
t  `RUN curl ... | sha256sum -c` pattern.\n   187\t- **No baked secrets.** The D
ockerfile MUST NOT declare ENV values\n   188\t  whose key names contain `TOKEN`
, `PASSWORD`, `SECRET`, `API_KEY`,\n   189\t  `PRIVATE_KEY`, `SIGNING_KEY`, or `
DSN`. Secrets are supplied by\n   190\t  the operator at runtime through environ
ment variables, never\n   191\t  baked into the image.\n   192\t- **No package i
nstall in the runtime stage.** `apt-get`,\n   193\t  `apt install`, `yum install
`, `dnf install`, `microdnf install`,\n   194\t  and `apk add` are rejected in t
he final layer. The builder stage\n   195\t  is free to install build dependenci
es; the runtime stage is not.\n   196\t- **`COPY --from=builder --chown=nonroot:
nonroot`.** Every\n   197\t  cross-stage COPY into the runtime layer MUST chown 
to the\n   198\t  non-root user so the copied artefact is not owned by root.\n  
199\t- **Explicit `ENTRYPOINT`.** The runtime stage MUST declare an\n   200\t  `
