ance the operator promotes\n   212\t   afterwards.\n   213\t4. **Restore the sna
pshot**: `pg_restore --clean --if-exists\n   214\t   --no-owner --no-acl --jobs=
4 -d <fresh-dsn> <snapshot>`. The snapshot\n   215\t   filename names the timest
amp; the restore-operator role\'s IAM principal\n   216\t   is the only one with
read access to the bucket.\n   217\t5. **Replay WAL**: if the restore point is l
ater than the snapshot,\n   218\t   continue WAL replay until `recovery_target_t
ime` matches the chosen\n   219\t   point. WAL retention covers the last 48 hour
s.\n   220\t6. **Apply migrations**: run `yalla-api --migrate-only` against the\
n   221\t   restored DSN. The applied migration version must match what the API\
n   222\t   binary expects; a mismatch aborts the restore.\n   223\t7. **Smoke-t
est**: run the canary suite (`scripts/canary.sh <restored-dsn>`)\n   224\t   whi
ch exercises one read from every public endpoint family. The smoke\n   225\t   t
est is required to pass before traffic is switched.\n   226\t8. **Switch traffic
**: update the API\'s `YALLA_DATABASE_URL` (or the secret\n   227\t   ref) to po
int at the restored DSN, then `kubectl rollout restart deploy\n   228\t   yalla-
api`. Confirm `/readyz` flips to ready before any worker is\n   229\t   resumed.
